    },
    {
      "_type": "UMLActivity",
      "_id": "8450159e00284a46963b6d48614d5b82",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "6e332ecd2a474fb2a9d9ae62a07d86c0"
      },
      "name": "AD-06 - Report & Resolve Incorrect Information",
      "visibility": "public",
      "isAbstract": false,
      "isReadOnly": false,
      "isSingleExecution": false,
      "documentation": "Activity Diagram derived from UC-14 (Report Incorrect Information) and UC-15 (Review/Resolve Report).\n\nShows the workflow through which a Reporter (Patient, Caregiver, Pharmacist, or Pharmacy Staff) submits a report about potentially incorrect medicine availability or price information, MedAccess validates and records the report, and an Authorized Reviewer (Administrator as primary reviewer; Pharmacist or Pharmacy Staff where authorized) investigates and resolves it.\n\nPreconditions:\n1. The reporter can identify the relevant medicine/pharmacy information.\n2. For review: the reviewer is authenticated and a report exists.\n\nPostconditions (success): The report is submitted, validated, recorded with a timestamp, and assigned a reviewable status; an authorized reviewer investigates it and the report is resolved or otherwise appropriately tracked, with resolution/status, reviewer identity, and timestamp recorded for auditability.\nPostconditions (alternative): The report is incomplete and the reporter is asked to provide required information; OR the would-be reviewer is unauthorized and access is denied; OR evidence is insufficient and the report is marked for further review / left unresolved.\n\nBusiness rules:\n- Submitting a report never itself changes stock or price information.\n- An unauthorized user cannot review or resolve a report.\n- Insufficient evidence does not force a resolution; the report may remain unresolved or be marked for further review.\n- Resolution/status, reviewer identity, and timestamp are always recorded, whether the report is resolved or left for further review.\n\nScope boundary: MedAccess records, routes, and tracks reports and their review outcomes. It does not diagnose, prescribe, recommend treatment, change dosage, automatically substitute medicines, or automatically change stock/price as a result of a report.\n\nTraceability: AD-06 -> UC-14 - Report Incorrect Information; UC-15 - Review/Resolve Report; FR-28-FR-31.",
      "ownedElements": [
